# Kavacha patch 0059 — Settings was dead: a duplicate `const lazy` took out
# every pane after the Privacy Center, and nothing stopped it.
#
# SYMPTOM, as reported: "i cant see any settings menu ... even when i click on
# certain settings it doesnt do anything". about:preferences opened and drew
# its chrome, so it did not look like a load failure — but the four Kavacha
# categories were absent and later panes were inert.
#
# THE BUG, in one line: every pane script in about:preferences is a classic
# <script> sharing ONE global scope, and both search.js (upstream) and
# kavacha-privacy.js declared `const lazy` at top level. Two top-level `const`
# bindings of the same name in one scope is a SyntaxError, so the whole of
# kavacha-privacy.js failed to PARSE — nothing in it ever ran.
#
# WHY THAT WAS CATASTROPHIC RATHER THAN LOCAL, which is the actually
# interesting part: a parse failure leaves gKavachaPrivacyCenter undefined, and
# init_all() called
#     register_module("paneKavachaPrivacy", gKavachaPrivacyCenter);
# with a bare global reference. That throws ReferenceError, which aborts
# init_all() — so EVERY pane registered after that line silently never
# initialised: the other three Kavacha panes, Firefox Labs, and Account & Sync.
# One duplicated identifier in one file disabled most of the Settings UI, and
# the only trace was two lines in the browser console.
#
# THE FIX IS TWO PARTS, deliberately:
#
#   1. Rename the binding to kavachaLazy. This alone restores everything. A
#      comment at the declaration says why the name is not `lazy`, because the
#      next person adding a top-level const here would otherwise reintroduce it.
#
#   2. Register the Zen/Kavacha panes through a guarded helper that checks
#      `typeof` first and try/catches register_module. This is the part worth
#      keeping even though (1) fixes today's failure: the blast radius was the
#      real defect. A broken pane must cost ONE pane, not every pane after it
#      in the list. Now a missing global logs "pane X is unavailable" and the
#      rest of Settings still builds.
#
# WHY IT WAS NOT CAUGHT: patches 0047–0050 were verified by reading the code
# and by checking that their strings/ids reached the package — REMAINING_WORK.md
# said in as many words that they were "complete on paper only" and that only a
# real session could settle them. This is exactly the class of defect that
# survives a static check: every file was present, every id was correct, and
# the feature was dead. Loading about:preferences once would have caught it.
#
# COLLISION AUDIT: scanned every classic pane script in the preferences scope
# for duplicate top-level const/let/var/class/function names. `lazy` was the
# only collision in the tree.
#
# FILES
#   src/browser/components/preferences/kavacha-privacy.js    lazy -> kavachaLazy
#   src/browser/components/preferences/preferences-js.patch  guarded registration
#
# VERIFIED against the built browser over Marionette, on the reporter's own
# profile: about:preferences loads with zero console errors (previously two);
# all four Kavacha categories present and visible; navigating to each expands
# its template and populates it (7/5/4/7 content nodes, 39 controls total);
# category-sync visible again.
diff --git a/src/browser/components/preferences/kavacha-privacy.js b/src/browser/components/preferences/kavacha-privacy.js
--- a/src/browser/components/preferences/kavacha-privacy.js
+++ b/src/browser/components/preferences/kavacha-privacy.js
@@ -19,8 +19,18 @@
